# SRG-APP-000770-AU-000170  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must implement a report generation capability that
# supports on-demand reporting requirements.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000770-AU-000170
group:           V-263563
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003826
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Splunk sets both report dispatch and report delivery in configuration,
                 which is what carries a report generation capability past ad hoc search
                 into support for a standing reporting requirement.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email in 1|true
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.to non_empty
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.sendpdf https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] schedule_window https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Recipients, reporting cycle and report format are organization-defined
                 parameters recorded in the system security plan.
external:        SMTP relay reachability, relay credentials and actual delivery rest on the
                 mail infrastructure and the network.
external:        The delivered form of a report, which is organization-defined and spread
                 across five savedsearches.conf switches and alert_actions.conf, so no
                 single key carries it.

citation:        savedsearches.conf.spec:73 enableSched = [0|1] default 0, :79
                 cron_schedule, :193 schedule_window = <unsigned integer> | auto, :300
                 action.email = <boolean> default false, :304 action.email.to = <email
                 list> "REQUIRED", :383 action.email.sendpdf = [1|0] default 0;
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:157 [email].
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: a report defined to satisfy an
                 audit reporting requirement is not dispatched on a stated cycle, or names
                 no recipients, so the application's report generation capability does not
                 support the reporting requirement.
